+# Experimental Vortex adapter
+
+`CUDF_NDSH_WITH_VORTEX=ON` adds local-file Parquet/Vortex comparisons for
+Q1/Q5/Q6/Q9/Q10 and projected reads. Default **OFF** adds no Vortex dependency.
+
+The main patch touches only `cpp/benchmarks/ndsh/` plus one include hook in
+`cpp/benchmarks/CMakeLists.txt`; no generator changes or generator-test target.
+
+17 offline tests, five-query clang-format, Ruff lint/format, and patch checks passed.
+Compile-only Q1/Q5/Q6/Q9/Q10 checks with Vortex ON/OFF passed **10/10 without warnings**;
+the separate generator regression test also compiled, without runtime execution.
+Artifacts are in the Vortex checkout's ignored `build/cudf-ndsh-minimal-compile/`.
+
+**Development binaries remain stale:** no CMake regeneration, full build, relinks, GPU,
+or fresh minimal-source runtime/memcheck/performance runs. The previous full cuDF build
+timed out at 1200 s / 223 of 635 steps. No broad automatic retry. Commands below are
+setup instructions, not evidence of completed runtime validation.
+
+## Build
+
+Use a complete local Vortex checkout with CUDA-layout edition registration,
+device decimal slicing, bitmap alignment/padding, dictionary export, and
+`vx_cuda_scan_path_arrow_device_stream_projected`. The retained pin lacks these fixes;
+publish a fixed revision before removing the local-only gate. The header-flag
+check alone does not verify all runtime fixes.
+
+From the cuDF root in a RAPIDS development environment:
+
+```sh
+cmake -S cpp -B cpp/build-vortex -G Ninja \
+  -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release \
+  -DBUILD_TESTS=OFF -DBUILD_BENCHMARKS=ON \
+  -DCUDF_NDSH_WITH_VORTEX=ON \
+  -DFETCHCONTENT_SOURCE_DIR_VORTEX=/absolute/path/to/updated/vortex \
+  -DCMAKE_CUDA_ARCHITECTURES=90
+CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=4 cmake --build cpp/build-vortex \
+  --target NDSH_VORTEX_BUILD_SMOKE NDSH_VORTEX_IO_TEST \
+    NDSH_Q01_NVBENCH NDSH_Q05_NVBENCH NDSH_Q06_NVBENCH \
+    NDSH_Q09_NVBENCH NDSH_Q10_NVBENCH --parallel 2
+cpp/build-vortex/benchmarks/NDSH_VORTEX_BUILD_SMOKE
+cpp/build-vortex/benchmarks/NDSH_VORTEX_IO_TEST
+compute-sanitizer --tool memcheck --error-exitcode 99 \
+  cpp/build-vortex/benchmarks/NDSH_VORTEX_IO_TEST
+```
+
+Requires Linux, Rust 1.95+, libclang, CUDA, and matching cuDF headers/libraries.
+Choose your GPU architecture (`90` is Hopper). Use a consistent compiler/sysroot
+and toolkit; set `CMAKE_CUDA_COMPILER`, `CUDAToolkit_ROOT`, and Cargo's `NVCC_CCBIN`
+when needed. Check Conda's `NVCC_PREPEND_FLAGS` for conflicts.
+
+Uncached dependencies need network access. Vortex uses its own CUB/nvCOMP;
+keep the Cargo build tree intact because runtime libraries are not packaged here.
+
+## Query comparisons
+
+```sh
+cpp/build-vortex/benchmarks/NDSH_Q01_NVBENCH \
+  --benchmark ndsh_q1_local --axis scale_factor=0.01 --axis 'cache=[warm,cold]' \
+  --min-samples 3 --timeout 3 --json q1-sf001.json
+cpp/build-vortex/benchmarks/NDSH_Q05_NVBENCH \
+  --benchmark ndsh_q5_local --axis scale_factor=0.01 --axis 'cache=[warm,cold]' \
+  --min-samples 3 --timeout 3 --json q5-sf001.json
+cpp/build-vortex/benchmarks/NDSH_Q06_NVBENCH \
+  --benchmark ndsh_q6_local --axis scale_factor=0.01 --axis 'cache=[warm,cold]' \
+  --min-samples 3 --timeout 3 --json q6-sf001.json
+cpp/build-vortex/benchmarks/NDSH_Q09_NVBENCH \
+  --benchmark ndsh_q9_local --axis scale_factor=0.01 --axis 'cache=[warm,cold]' \
+  --min-samples 3 --timeout 3 --json q9-sf001.json
+cpp/build-vortex/benchmarks/NDSH_Q10_NVBENCH \
+  --benchmark ndsh_q10_local --axis scale_factor=0.01 --axis 'cache=[warm,cold]' \
+  --min-samples 3 --timeout 3 --json q10-sf001.json
+```
+
+Each runs `format={parquet,vortex}` × `workload={read,qN}` × `cache={warm,cold}` on
+identical logical full-table fixtures from the **original pinned cuDF generator**;
+Q9 additionally covers binary-op, AST, and transform amount engines. The default scale
+factors include SF10; select a scale explicitly. Q1/Q6 project lineitem, Q5/Q9 project
+six tables, and Q10 projects four. Both formats use identical scan projections and
+post-read predicates. Exact projection/value and independent bounded-batch CPU result
+checks remain even for zero matches, as do synthetic nonempty and boundary/null/empty
+cases. Checks/writing are untimed; read/query timing includes cleanup and GPU completion.
+Compare CPU wall time; RMM peaks exclude Vortex. Original native Parquet-pushdown/output
+benchmarks remain separate. References follow those benchmark semantics; Q9 keeps its
+existing unrounded `SUM(amount)`. Q1 uses original `SUM`/native `MEAN`/`COUNT` and
+Q5/Q9/Q10 table reads are sequential in both formats. Native Parquet benchmarks retain
+input/intermediate lifetimes through output writing. No hand-fitted query kernels.
+
+Original data may yield empty/degenerate Q6/Q10 and low-SF supplier joins. Explicit zero
+match counts disclose these results without rejecting them or skipping correctness
+checks. Degenerate queries are **not meaningful full-query performance evidence**.
+Q6 checks zero-match `SUM` is NULL and reports revenue as the string `"NULL"`, not zero.
+Its CPU reference boundary/sliced/float32 test moved to `q06.cpp` and gained no-match/empty
+GPU cases; generator separation loses no main-query tests. Q9's reference preserves
+`partsupp` duplicate-join multiplicity, with matching/unmatched duplicate cases. These
+cases compiled but have not been run on the minimal source.
+
+Cold mode flushes and evicts each selected-format fixture from the Linux page cache,
+then requires zero resident pages before every timed callback. Eviction is untimed.
+Vortex uses direct I/O for cold data reads; metadata stays buffered. Parquet uses its
+native reader. Lower-level storage caches are not flushed: this is OS-page-cache
+coldness, not guaranteed cold media. Warm reads use the buffered path.
+
+**Optional generator patch:** the main `upstream.patch` has no generator edits/tests
+or `NDSH_DATA_GENERATOR_TEST` target. Vortex's optional
+`benchmarks/cudf-ndsh/generator-fixes.patch` preserves four independent fixes and its
+own regression test across seven files. It is separately reviewable and independently
+applicable to cuDF pin `5339497a1a17d799687cbf189fb113411fb015ca`, not bundled or automatic.
+Its forward application to pristine cuDF passed; both patch application orders produce
+identical trees. Only it adds `NDSH_DATA_GENERATOR_TEST`. Applying it affects all NDS-H
+consumers, including Vortex OFF: regenerate both formats' fixtures and label the dataset
+as generator-fixed. Neither dataset establishes full TPC-H conformance.
+
+**Prior timings are HISTORICAL, not valid minimal-patch baselines:** they used altered
+generator/performance code and event suppression. Restoring the original source/data
+requires regenerating both formats' fixtures and collecting fresh labeled baselines;
+optional generator-fixed data also needs separate baselines. Preserve old evidence
+tables as historical, not current validation.
+
+## Contract and scope
+
+- `write_vortex`: cuDF chunks → compact host Arrow → CPU-compressed local file.
+  The benchmark uses 16,777,216-row physical CUDA-flat blocks. Explicit row blocks
+  disable byte coalescing and layout dictionaries so high-cardinality `u16` dictionary
+  runs cannot fragment the requested granularity.
+- `read_vortex`: pooled cacheable pinned-host staging → HtoD → GPU decode → retained Arrow Device
+  imports → one final owning cuDF copy/concatenation, using the same 16,777,216-row
+  maximum. The adapter retains up to 8 GiB in CUDA's default memory pool between
+  synchronized reads. Dictionary-compressed arrays export as plain values.
+  These Vortex-internal improvements remain; no event optimization is retained.
+  **No GPUDirect Storage.**
+- Contexts use device 0. Caller stream/resource must outlive the
+  context and returned tables. Reads finish consumer work before releasing temporary
+  inputs; release cleanup may remain queued on Vortex producer streams. Results outlive
+  the context/file. See `vortex_io.hpp` for argument constraints.
+- Flat typed columns and ordered top-level projection only. No predicate pushdown,
+  remote/device-buffer sources, GPU writing, or full RMM integration. Row chunking
+  is not a byte budget; peak read memory includes retained Vortex batches plus the
+  owning result.
+- Time the complete read, including schema export, import, final copy/concatenation,
+  release cleanup, and GPU completion; exclude writing. Query/read benchmarks finish
+  with a device-wide synchronization that includes queued producer cleanup. The adapter
+  emits `vortex.read`, `vortex.scan_open`, `vortex.get_next`,
+  `vortex.arrow_device_import`, `vortex.materialize`, `vortex.consumer_sync`, and
+  `vortex.release_batches` NVTX ranges. Tests establish correctness, not SF100 readiness.
+  For profiling, use `RelWithDebInfo` and optionally `NVCC_APPEND_FLAGS=-lineinfo`.
